00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:35.523
- Let's get into another question.

00:10:37.406 --> 00:10:40.430
Paola asks...

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:42.400
- Paola, isn't that some kind of like--

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:43.253
- Illegal thing?

00:10:44.544 --> 00:10:47.690
In another universe you guys are teachers.

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:50.890
What subject would you like to teach?

00:10:50.890 --> 00:10:53.421
My answer is pottery.

00:10:53.421 --> 00:10:56.190
Like I wanna be a thrower.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.710
Isn't that what they're called

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:01.321
when you're like spinning
pottery and then throwing it?

00:11:01.321 --> 00:11:03.411
It's called a thrower.

00:11:03.411 --> 00:11:04.610
- I have no idea.

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:07.242
- A person who pots, makes pots.

00:11:07.242 --> 00:11:09.587
Throws the--
- But you wanna be a teacher

00:11:09.587 --> 00:11:11.988
or you wanna be just a
person who makes pots

00:11:11.988 --> 00:11:13.953
because there's a distinct difference.

00:11:13.953 --> 00:11:17.700
- I actually don't think it is.

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:19.660
I wanna be a guy who makes pots

00:11:21.296 --> 00:11:24.207
in different mud stuff.

00:11:24.207 --> 00:11:26.290
- That's a craftsman.
- And so well

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:28.189
that I can teach people--

00:11:28.189 --> 00:11:30.070
- But what's more important--
- It seems like--

00:11:30.070 --> 00:11:31.370
- The crafting or the teaching?

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:33.460
- It seems like, well
I have to be a teacher.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:34.340
That's the question.

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:35.220
I wanna teach it.

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:37.010
I think it would be fun to teach.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:39.360
- You used the teaching question
as a way to get to a hobby

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.920
that you wanna make into
your job which is fine

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:44.948
but I find it interesting that
the teaching part is not--

00:11:44.948 --> 00:11:47.090
- I'll get to that.
- What appeals to you.

00:11:47.090 --> 00:11:50.400
- No I think that it's a,

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:53.680
teaching as a concept stresses me out.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:56.110
There's a lot of pressure associated with

00:11:57.740 --> 00:12:01.203
knowing something so
well to then tell people

00:12:01.203 --> 00:12:04.080
that stuff and then they're
supposed to believe it

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:06.930
and then impact their lives.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:08.903
That's just a lot of pressure.

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:13.280
I don't have that type of
confidence and knowledge.

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:16.250
I always feel like I
need to state everything

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.750
accoutred as an opinion and you know what,

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:20.356
I love to give opinions.

00:12:20.356 --> 00:12:21.530
- Oh really.
- On things where

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:24.570
there aren't answers, but
teaching something seems so final

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:27.400
and I feel like I can
screw up people's lives

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.763
unless it's just them making a pot.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:33.873
- Mm, but pots can be very,
very special to people.

00:12:33.873 --> 00:12:35.880
- I also think--
- Be very significant,

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:37.100
especially depends on what you put in 'em.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:38.361
- And I like that.

00:12:38.361 --> 00:12:41.560
So in form I'd like to be an art teacher

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:45.020
where it's not about, if
I'm wrong about something

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:47.340
that I've passed along
then somebody's gonna--

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:48.840
- That's interesting,
so the reason you went

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:51.540
to art is not because...

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:54.750
It's because you value the
subjective nature of art.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:57.270
You're afraid to teach
anything that might be

00:12:57.270 --> 00:13:01.278
considered to be objective
or final in some way.

00:13:01.278 --> 00:13:03.923
- I think that's what drew me
to it and also it seems like

00:13:03.923 --> 00:13:08.923
I think I could be a
zen teacher of pottery.

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:13.030
I think it could be...

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:18.023
My class would be equal
parts pottery and therapy.

00:13:20.262 --> 00:13:24.320
Inspirational, I wanna
have an inspirational class

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:27.220
where people are just touching mud.

00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:28.053
- Mm.

00:13:28.053 --> 00:13:31.478
- 'Cause it's like, it's very primal,

00:13:31.478 --> 00:13:36.478
playing with mud and dirt
and the spinning motion.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:39.280
It could be symbolic of
something that I would make up

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:41.560
just to get people excited.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.410
I just think there's a lot of potential.

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:45.540
- It sounds like you really
thought this through.

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:46.373
- Yeah.

00:13:48.615 --> 00:13:51.400
- As you know, I'm not--
- TED Talk, I mean,

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:53.360
I'll be making TED Talks about it.

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:56.914
- I am not, I don't hold back.

00:13:56.914 --> 00:14:00.040
I don't have a problem
with telling people things.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:01.610
- Yeah.

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:03.990
- In fact, well I've talked
about this many times before

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:07.400
but my dad's a law professor

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:11.060
and he loves,

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:12.430
not just teaching a class

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:15.240
because he also likes
telling you what he thinks

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:17.130
about things in the same way that I do.

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.050
- Yeah.
- He likes an audience.

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:21.090
If he wasn't a professor,
he'd be a stand-up comedian.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:23.440
It's like we have a
very similar personality

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:26.180
in a lot of ways and I
ended up being the comedian,

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:30.210
not the professor, but
I am not making this up.

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:35.210
I really, really want to
be a University professor

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.590
at some point in my life,
and I'm holding out hope

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:40.670
that there's gonna be some opportunity.

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:42.519
- You think you're gonna
get some honorary--

00:14:42.519 --> 00:14:44.300
- Yeah.
- YouTube degree?

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:49.127
- No to be able to be like,
oh, I'm gonna teach this

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:54.375
particular class for
this particular program

00:14:54.375 --> 00:14:56.730
because of something that is from my past

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:58.800
that qualifies me to do it in some way.

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:01.693
I don't know what it'll
be, 20 years from now.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:04.420
