the technology at the time.

00:35:15.640 --> 00:35:18.860
You should look this up,
just Google Peter Jackson

00:35:19.790 --> 00:35:24.430
war footage restoration and...

00:35:24.430 --> 00:35:27.570
I don't know what that was
for, but it is fascinating.

00:35:27.570 --> 00:35:28.733
What is that for?

00:35:31.410 --> 00:35:33.760
Oh it's for a movie he's working on?

00:35:33.760 --> 00:35:34.833
Is it the biopic?

00:35:36.260 --> 00:35:37.640
- Our biopic?

00:35:37.640 --> 00:35:39.210
- Starring Daniel Radcliffe and

00:35:41.330 --> 00:35:42.823
Lucas Lerman, Logan Lerman.

00:35:42.823 --> 00:35:45.460
- Okay I'm getting bored,
let me ask another question.

00:35:45.460 --> 00:35:49.066
Sa Jeuuh asks,

00:35:49.066 --> 00:35:54.066
if intelligent alien
life exists, and it does.

00:35:56.382 --> 00:35:59.279
What is the first thing
you would want to know

00:35:59.279 --> 00:36:01.670
about their civilization?

00:36:01.670 --> 00:36:04.497
I would want to know if they have music.

00:36:04.497 --> 00:36:05.443
#EarBiscuits.

00:36:08.493 --> 00:36:12.870
Okay so Sa would want to
know if they have music.

00:36:12.870 --> 00:36:15.464
I mean that is a particularly
specific question

00:36:15.464 --> 00:36:17.450
to ask at first.

00:36:17.450 --> 00:36:20.980
I think it's more of like,
once you know your life's not

00:36:20.980 --> 00:36:23.230
in danger and they're cool
and you're hanging out

00:36:23.230 --> 00:36:24.930
and you're just like, I don't know,

00:36:24.930 --> 00:36:26.670
hey let's grab a beer or let's--

00:36:26.670 --> 00:36:28.898
- That's quite a leap, but go ahead.

00:36:28.898 --> 00:36:30.200
- Huh?

00:36:30.200 --> 00:36:31.440
- That's quite a leap.

00:36:31.440 --> 00:36:33.260
- To say that they're friendly?

00:36:33.260 --> 00:36:36.480
- Well because my answer is
I wanna know their weakness.

00:36:36.480 --> 00:36:37.500
- Tell me your weakness.

00:36:37.500 --> 00:36:42.500
- Because I know, I don't care
how the initial meeting goes.

00:36:42.715 --> 00:36:47.340
The only way that, the only ending,

00:36:47.340 --> 00:36:50.970
the only potential ending
when two different species

00:36:50.970 --> 00:36:54.300
from different parts, alien
species from different parts

00:36:54.300 --> 00:36:56.570
of the universe come together,
the only way it will end

00:36:56.570 --> 00:36:59.492
is in the annihilation of
one of the people groups.

00:36:59.492 --> 00:37:01.700
- That's sad.
- That's just the rule

00:37:01.700 --> 00:37:03.418
of the universe, man, you have to assume

00:37:03.418 --> 00:37:05.410
that that is what's going to happen.

00:37:05.410 --> 00:37:09.260
Now we go in friendly,
handshakes, all of that,

00:37:09.260 --> 00:37:12.760
but just know, eventually,
it's gonna hit the fan

00:37:12.760 --> 00:37:14.095
and it's us or them.

00:37:14.095 --> 00:37:17.139
- I think you may be tipping
your hand a little bit,

00:37:17.139 --> 00:37:20.930
all four of 'em, if you ask the question

00:37:20.930 --> 00:37:23.480
what is your weakness,
so let's try to come up

00:37:23.480 --> 00:37:24.733
with another way to get at it.

00:37:24.733 --> 00:37:26.840
- Well he didn't say it was
a question, it was like,

00:37:26.840 --> 00:37:28.831
what is the first thing
you would want to know

00:37:28.831 --> 00:37:30.331
about their civilization.

00:37:30.331 --> 00:37:32.250
What is the Achilles heel?

00:37:32.250 --> 00:37:34.020
That's the question, I
wanna know what it is.

00:37:34.020 --> 00:37:36.890
Do they have some, is
there a core in the middle

00:37:36.890 --> 00:37:39.010
that we can drop a bomb
into that all of a sudden,

00:37:39.010 --> 00:37:42.080
the whole thing will explode
on itself like the Death Star,

00:37:42.080 --> 00:37:44.206
because if so, I wanna know what that is.

00:37:44.206 --> 00:37:45.720
- And then once you find that out,

00:37:45.720 --> 00:37:48.530
your second question is
like hey do you have music?

00:37:48.530 --> 00:37:49.700
- (chuckles) Do you have music?

00:37:49.700 --> 00:37:51.433
- I like the music question.

00:37:51.433 --> 00:37:53.440
- I think it's, did y'all
have music? (chuckles)

00:37:53.440 --> 00:37:55.960
Because we just blew you up. (chuckles)

00:37:55.960 --> 00:37:57.310
- Wow, you are...

00:37:59.207 --> 00:38:01.150
You are a bleak--
- Where's the black box?

00:38:01.150 --> 00:38:02.773
Is there music on it?

00:38:02.773 --> 00:38:05.070
(Link chuckles)

00:38:05.070 --> 00:38:06.700
I'm just a realist, man.

00:38:06.700 --> 00:38:11.678
- Just to keep the, just the
sub-thread of this thing,

00:38:11.678 --> 00:38:15.523
of this fire stoked,
my answer is gonna be,

00:38:16.553 --> 00:38:19.590
how do you do the naughty stuff?

00:38:19.590 --> 00:38:21.030
- Oh wow.

00:38:21.030 --> 00:38:22.862
You wanna see a demonstration?

00:38:22.862 --> 00:38:25.149
- Give me a demonstration if you must.

00:38:25.149 --> 00:38:28.870
Like I mean that's the only
part of Avatar I remember.

00:38:28.870 --> 00:38:30.450
How many--
- And it was tentacles

00:38:30.450 --> 00:38:31.490
or something right?

00:38:31.490 --> 00:38:32.380
What was it?

00:38:32.380 --> 00:38:37.080
- Yeah it was like a tentacle
intertwining of umbilicalness.

00:38:37.080 --> 00:38:38.400
- It didn't seem fun.

00:38:38.400 --> 00:38:40.370
There was no thrusting.

00:38:40.370 --> 00:38:41.410
- Come on now.

00:38:41.410 --> 00:38:44.680
Now, but yeah, I mean, and you know what,

00:38:44.680 --> 00:38:49.680
my question seems innocuous
but it could be the key

00:38:51.030 --> 00:38:52.537
to finding their weakness.
- It could be their weakness.

00:38:52.537 --> 00:38:54.403
- And so you just let
me do all the talking

00:38:54.403 --> 00:38:56.150
just like at all of our Hollywood parties.

00:38:56.150 --> 00:38:58.690
- Once all of them
tentacle up to each other,

00:38:58.690 --> 00:39:01.106
that's when we kill 'em all. (chuckles)

00:39:01.106 --> 00:39:03.633
- (chuckles) Gosh, you're horrible.

00:39:04.660 --> 00:39:06.370
- Once you guys all get
attached to each other

00:39:06.370 --> 00:39:09.640
and start procreating,
we're going to blow you up.

00:39:09.640 --> 00:39:11.150
I mean it's real sick.

00:39:11.150 --> 00:39:13.143
Oh hold on there is thrusting.

00:39:13.143 --> 00:39:14.580
He just brought the video up.

00:39:14.580 --> 00:39:17.220
Well there was one thrust in
particular it looked like.

00:39:17.220 --> 00:39:18.180
- I'm just--

00:39:18.180 --> 00:39:20.200
- Avatar's coming back,
you know about that, right?

00:39:20.200 --> 00:39:21.760
He's been working on that forever.

00:39:21.760 --> 00:39:24.151
- Oh gosh, yeah there's
gonna be four of 'em.

00:39:24.151 --> 00:39:27.860
- We got a buddy who
lives pretty close to us

00:39:27.860 --> 00:39:32.740
who has been traveling all the
way down to Manhattan Beach

00:39:32.740 --> 00:39:35.269
I think is where they've
been working on it

00:39:35.269 --> 00:39:37.440
who's been doing a lot of the costumes.

00:39:37.440 --> 00:39:40.130
- Costume designing on all the Avatars.

00:39:40.130 --> 00:39:42.086
- But the funny thing is I was like,

00:39:42.086 --> 00:39:43.314
well what are you working on now?

00:39:43.314 --> 00:39:44.700
He said, "Well, I'm doing some,"

00:39:44.700 --> 00:39:47.010
and he's not like a stylist.

00:39:47.010 --> 00:39:49.439
He literally is drawing the stuff.

00:39:49.439 --> 00:39:50.760
- Yeah.

00:39:50.760 --> 00:39:54.330
- And this is like, this is
his job for like a decade.

00:39:54.330 --> 00:39:55.940
That's (chuckles), you
know what I'm saying.

00:39:55.940 --> 00:39:58.652
Once you start working on
that, that's just what you do.

00:39:58.652 --> 00:39:59.880
- Yeah once you start
working with him, yeah.

00:39:59.880 --> 00:40:02.270
- Because he's just got so much stuff.

00:40:02.270 --> 00:40:03.720
- What's his name?

00:40:03.720 --> 00:40:05.810
- James Cameron.
- James Cameron,

00:40:05.810 --> 00:40:07.810
the deep sea diver.

00:40:07.810 --> 00:40:08.810
- That's our friend.

00:40:11.161 --> 00:40:13.100
We got a friend who's working on Avatar.

00:40:13.100 --> 00:40:17.169
His names is James Cameron.
(Link laughs)

00:40:17.169 --> 00:40:19.551
Jim Cameron, yeah we called him Jimmy.

00:40:19.551 --> 00:40:21.713
- (chuckles) Jimmy Cam.

00:40:21.713 --> 00:40:24.296
(both chuckle)

00:40:25.939 --> 00:40:27.810
(Rhett sighs)

00:40:27.810 --> 00:40:29.945
- Having fun today, Link.
- What is your weakness,

00:40:29.945 --> 00:40:31.940
James Cameron?

00:40:31.940 --> 00:40:33.730
- Jennifer Flores.

00:40:33.730 --> 00:40:37.610
If you could instantaneously
give yourself a quality

00:40:37.610 --> 00:40:41.390
you don't already possess,
example desire to clean,

00:40:41.390 --> 00:40:44.450
photographic memory,
write poetry, breakdance,

00:40:44.450 --> 00:40:45.590
what would it be?

00:40:45.590 --> 00:40:47.780
Now keep in mind this is not a superpower.

00:40:47.780 --> 00:40:49.550
We're not talking about
something that doesn't exist.

00:40:49.550 --> 00:40:51.360
- This question matters.
- This is a quality

00:40:51.360 --> 00:40:53.780
that humans can have

00:40:53.780 --> 00:40:57.960
and you could, through a
combination of natural talent

00:40:57.960 --> 00:41:01.850
and practice, get
straight-up, but this is just,

00:41:01.850 --> 00:41:03.030
you can snap your fingers
and you can get it.

00:41:03.030 --> 00:41:04.880
What would it be?
- Instantaneously.

00:41:06.387 --> 00:41:11.387
You know since we're
working on music and stuff,

00:41:11.730 --> 00:41:13.690
this isn't my answer,
but I was thinking like--

00:41:13.690 --> 00:41:15.178
- You're gonna take my answer.

00:41:15.178 --> 00:41:18.002
- Something in the music
world but I actually,

00:41:18.002 --> 00:41:20.790
I stopped that 'cause I
didn't wanna go there.

00:41:20.790 --> 00:41:21.630
- Okay.

00:41:21.630 --> 00:41:25.473
- I applaud your efforts
in learning the piano.

00:41:27.030 --> 00:41:29.723
As we gear up for concerts.

00:41:29.723 --> 00:41:33.826
- And I think that's why my
answer was to be a virtuoso.

00:41:33.826 --> 00:41:36.400
- Oh, on a piano?
- Well, so--

00:41:36.400 --> 00:41:38.062
- On any instrument?

00:41:38.062 --> 00:41:40.060
'Cause my answer is
different but go ahead.

00:41:40.060 --> 00:41:45.060
- Well, if it's an option
to be a musical virtuoso

00:41:45.518 --> 00:41:48.350
of all instruments, which,
I mean there are people

00:41:48.350 --> 00:41:51.300
who can play a lot of, but
that's kind of multiple skills.

00:41:51.300 --> 00:41:52.830
So I would definitely do that but if I had

00:41:52.830 --> 00:41:56.180
to choose one instrument
and this is probably

00:41:56.180 --> 00:41:57.880
because I'm just beginning to learn,

00:41:57.880 --> 00:41:59.600
I do think it would be the piano.

00:41:59.600 --> 00:42:00.452
- Yeah.

00:42:00.452 --> 00:42:02.750
- 'Cause I just think
that what you can explore

00:42:02.750 --> 00:42:05.379
on the piano is just limitless.

00:42:05.379 --> 00:42:08.750
- I was sitting down,
Lando called me over,

00:42:08.750 --> 00:42:10.477
he was like, "Tell me, do you prefer it

00:42:10.477 --> 00:42:12.367
"when I play this song
like this or like this

00:42:12.367 --> 00:42:15.357
"because I'm encouraged,"
he didn't use the word,

00:42:15.357 --> 00:42:17.810
"She told me I can change
it any way I want,"

00:42:17.810 --> 00:42:19.160
and he played it two different ways

00:42:19.160 --> 00:42:23.100
and I was just so envious
and proud of the way

00:42:23.100 --> 00:42:27.300
that he was able to move his
fingers across the ivories.

00:42:27.300 --> 00:42:32.300
And he's actually learned to,
whenever he feels overwhelmed

00:42:35.060 --> 00:42:39.270
or anxious, he will go over
to the piano and start playing

00:42:39.270 --> 00:42:42.963
and it's a calming,

00:42:44.440 --> 00:42:45.610
a calming effect.

00:42:45.610 --> 00:42:47.210
- Does it come out in the music?

00:42:49.228 --> 00:42:51.633
Is he like, this is my angry song.

00:42:53.250 --> 00:42:56.590
- No, it's more of a
calming, he always plays like

00:42:56.590 --> 00:42:58.648
a calming thing which he's,

00:42:58.648 --> 00:43:01.250
one of the songs that he's working on now.

00:43:01.250 --> 00:43:04.300
But just the level with
which you can get in touch

00:43:04.300 --> 00:43:08.650
with, it's just a connectivity
to a different part

00:43:08.650 --> 00:43:10.630
of your brain and body

00:43:10.630 --> 00:43:15.060
that I am envious of,
especially with the piano,

00:43:15.060 --> 00:43:18.350
the way there's a lot
of physicality with it

00:43:18.350 --> 00:43:21.280
and it's like a full body experience.

00:43:21.280 --> 00:43:22.750
Are you experiencing
that as you're learning

00:43:22.750 --> 00:43:24.009
to play the piano?

00:43:24.009 --> 00:43:25.641
Is it--
- I'm not--

00:43:25.641 --> 00:43:27.160
- I know it's early.

00:43:27.160 --> 00:43:29.390
- Well the funny thing
about this and you will,

00:43:29.390 --> 00:43:31.440
if you come to the London show or you come

00:43:31.440 --> 00:43:33.840
to any of the shows that
are booked for 2019,

00:43:33.840 --> 00:43:36.318
you will see me play the piano.

00:43:36.318 --> 00:43:39.940
